-- Plan for the blueprint projector and build-control (see lib/plan.lua):
-- a Lua plan returns the same table a JSON plan holds, made by code.
--
-- Mega pagoda: a many-roofed timber pagoda in a moss garden, 73x93 and
-- 89 high, from the structure file mega_pegoda_turtleking.nbt. Uses blocks
-- from Oh The Biomes We've Gone (white mangrove), Fetzi's Asian Deco
-- (framed fences, built plain: their frame texture isn't kept) and
-- Torchmaster (feral flare lanterns; their invisible lights are left out,
-- the lanterns place them). Chest contents and mobs aren't kept.
--
-- The blocks are packed to keep the file small: PALETTE lists every block
-- (no "minecraft:" prefix on vanilla ones), and each LAYERS string is one
-- layer, bottom first, cells north row first, west to east, 73 per row.
-- Each cell is a palette letter ("~" or "^" before a letter: the next
-- 75 or the ones after), "." for air, and a number in front repeats it.
